n","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Minnesota fires OC Greg Harbaugh Jr., ending third stint with Gophers","description":"Minnesota fired offensive coordinator Greg Harbaugh Jr. as the Golden Gophers rank 15th in the Big Ten in scoring and 17th in yards per game.","published":"2026-11-15T19:36:27.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50491908/minnesota-fires-oc-greg-harbaugh-jr-ending-3rd-gophers-stint","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Allstate Playoff Predictor","description":"Select your favorite contender, make your picks for how its season will play out and see what the Allstate Playoff Predictor foretells.","published":"2026-11-15T18:13:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/feature/story/_/page/cfbplayoffpredictor/college-football-allstate-playoff-bracket-predictor","type":"Eticket","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft questions, latest intel, risers, CFB standouts","description":"Is Jackson Harris the WR3 in the class? And has Boubacar Traore emerged as the No. 3 edge rusher? Here's our weekly draft spin, including top standouts.","published":"2026-11-15T17:34:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49881131/2027-nfl-draft-risers-questions-college-football-prospects","type":"Story","byline":"Mel Kiper Jr. and Jordan Reid","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870874/lawson-luckie","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawson_Luckie"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Lawson Luckie","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawson_Luckie","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:23Z","intro":"Lawson Luckie (born October 21, 2004) is an American college football tight end for the Georgia Bulldogs of the Southeastern Conference (SEC).","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Luckie grew up in Norcross, Georgia, and attended Norcross High School. He accumulated 728 all-purpose yards as a senior. Luckie was rated a four-star recruit and committed to play college football at Georgia over offers from Alabama, Auburn, Florida State, LSU, Ole Miss, and Texas A&M."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Luckie joined the Georgia Bulldogs as an early enrollee in December 2022 and took part in the team's practices leading up to the 2022 Peach Bowl. He played in seven games as a true freshman and caught two passes for nine yards and one touchdown."}]}}